---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Two Keys to the Womb — Daf Yomi Game: Bekhorot 19"
  description="Bekhorot 19: drop newborns through three verse-sieves, turn the two keys of a firstborn for Rabbi Tarfon and Rabbi Akiva, fire counterexamples at Ravina, draw Rabbi Yishmael's age lines for an animal bought from a gentile, and find out which majorities the Rabbis follow."
>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link
    rel="stylesheet"
    href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Frank+Ruhl+Libre:wght@400;500;700;900&display=swap"
  />

  <main class="frank min-h-screen bg-[#16121a] !text-[#eee6ef]">
    <!-- ============ Hero ============ -->
    <header class="px-4 pt-12 pb-8">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl">
        <p class="text-sm !text-[#a596a8]">
          <a href="/daf" class="underline decoration-[#4a3d4e] hover:!text-[#e3a86c]">Daf Yomi Arcade</a>, Bekhorot 19, 7 October 2026
        </p>
        <h1 class="mt-3 text-5xl font-black leading-[1.05] sm:text-6xl">Two Keys to the Womb</h1>
        <p class="mt-3 text-2xl !text-[#e3a86c]" dir="rtl" lang="he">בְּכוֹר לְדָבָר אֶחָד לָא הָוֵי בְּכוֹר</p>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-xl text-lg leading-relaxed !text-[#d8cdd9]">
          The Torah calls the firstborn both <em>bekhor</em>, "first," and <em>peter reḥem</em>, "the one that
          opens the womb." Usually they're the same animal. Today's daf asks what happens when a caesarean birth
          splits them apart, and then buys a goat from a gentile who can't say whether she has ever given birth.
        </p>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 600 90" class="mt-6 w-full" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M10 76 H590" stroke="#4a3d4e" stroke-width="2" />
          <path d="M250 76 V30 a50 50 0 0 1 100 0 V76" fill="none" stroke="#7b5f84" stroke-width="4" />
          <g fill="#e3a86c">
            <circle cx="150" cy="44" r="13" fill="none" stroke="#e3a86c" stroke-width="5" /><rect x="161" y="41" width="56" height="6" /><rect x="203" y="47" width="6" height="11" /><rect x="192" y="47" width="6" height="8" />
          </g>
          <g fill="#8fbfa6">
            <circle cx="450" cy="44" r="13" fill="none" stroke="#8fbfa6" stroke-width="5" /><rect x="383" y="41" width="56" height="6" /><rect x="391" y="47" width="6" height="11" /><rect x="402" y="47" width="6" height="8" />
          </g>
          <text x="300" y="62" text-anchor="middle" font-size="22" fill="#eee6ef">?</text>
          <text x="150" y="86" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" fill="#a596a8">first out</text>
          <text x="450" y="86" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" fill="#a596a8">opens the womb</text>
        </svg>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 pb-20">
      <!-- ============ Part I: sieves ============ -->
      <section class="border-t border-[#3a2f3e] pt-8" aria-labelledby="p1">
        <h2 id="p1" class="text-3xl font-bold">I. Three sieves</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed !text-[#d8cdd9]">
          A baraita builds the definition of a firstborn out of a general term and a detail that need each other.
          Each phrase is a sieve that catches one kind of newborn the others would let through. Drop each newborn
          and choose the sieve that catches it, or send it all the way through to the kohen.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 space-y-1.5 rounded-lg border border-[#3a2f3e] bg-[#1d1822] p-4 text-sm">
          <p><span class="sv">A</span> <span dir="rtl" lang="he" class="text-lg">״קַדֶּשׁ לִי כׇל בְּכוֹר״</span>: "all the <b>firstborn</b>" (Exodus 13:2)</p>
          <p><span class="sv">B</span> <span dir="rtl" lang="he" class="text-lg">״הַזָּכָר״</span>: "every firstborn <b>male</b>" (Deuteronomy 15:19)</p>
          <p><span class="sv">C</span> <span dir="rtl" lang="he" class="text-lg">״פֶּטֶר כׇּל רֶחֶם״</span>: "that which <b>opens</b> any womb" (Exodus 13:2)</p>
        </div>
        <div id="sieve" class="mt-5 space-y-4"></div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ Part II: keys ============ -->
      <section class="mt-12 border-t border-[#3a2f3e] pt-8" aria-labelledby="p2">
        <h2 id="p2" class="text-3xl font-bold">II. The caesarean and the one after it</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed !text-[#d8cdd9]">
          The mishna: a male is born by caesarean section (<span dir="rtl" lang="he">יוֹצֵא דּוֹפֶן</span>), then a
          second male is born through the womb. Each one holds only one of the two keys. Pick a judge, then rule
          on both animals.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-5 grid grid-cols-2 gap-3">
          <div class="rounded-lg border border-[#3a2f3e] bg-[#1d1822] p-3 text-center">
            <p class="font-bold">Caesarean male</p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm"><span class="key on">🗝 first out</span></p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-sm"><span class="key off">🗝 opens the womb</span></p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-lg border border-[#3a2f3e] bg-[#1d1822] p-3 text-center">
            <p class="font-bold">Male after it</p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm"><span class="key off">🗝 first out</span></p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-sm"><span class="key on g">🗝 opens the womb</span></p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div id="keys" class="mt-5 space-y-5"></div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ Part III: theories ============ -->
      <section class="mt-12 border-t border-[#3a2f3e] pt-8" aria-labelledby="p3">
        <h2 id="p3" class="text-3xl font-bold">III. Fire a counterexample</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed !text-[#d8cdd9]">
          Rav Sherevya spots something odd in the sieve baraita. To exclude a male born after a female, it uses
          sieve C ("opens the womb") instead of sieve A ("firstborn"). To exclude the male after a caesarean, it uses
          A. Does one key count as a firstborn or not?
        </p>
        <div id="theory" class="mt-5 space-y-5"></div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ Part IV: age lines ============ -->
      <section class="mt-12 border-t border-[#3a2f3e] pt-8" aria-labelledby="p4">
        <h2 id="p4" class="text-3xl font-bold">IV. Bought from a gentile</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed !text-[#d8cdd9]">
          New mishna: you buy a female animal from a gentile who can't tell you whether she has ever given birth.
          Now she bears a male. Rabbi Yishmael says that if she is young enough, the male is <em>certainly</em> the
          kohen's; past that age it's a doubt. For each species, tap the last year of age that's still certain.
        </p>
        <div id="ages" class="mt-5 space-y-3"></div>
        <button id="ageCheck" class="act mt-4">Draw the lines</button>
        <div id="ageOut" class="mt-3 space-y-3 text-sm" aria-live="polite"></div>
        <div id="akiva" class="mt-6 space-y-5"></div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ Part V: majority ============ -->
      <section class="mt-12 border-t border-[#3a2f3e] pt-8" aria-labelledby="p5">
        <h2 id="p5" class="text-3xl font-bold">V. A majority you can see</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed !text-[#d8cdd9]">
          The Gemara asks: why is an older goat only a doubt? Most animals conceive and give birth within their
          first year, so follow the majority. Its first answer is that the Rabbis only follow a majority that is
          "in front of us" (<span dir="rtl" lang="he">רוּבָּא דְּאִיתֵיהּ קַמַּן</span>). Picture a piece of meat lying
          in the street:
        </p>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 400 92" class="mt-4 w-full" role="img" aria-label="Ten shops: nine kosher, one not, with a piece of meat in the street">
          <g id="shops"></g>
          <path d="M0 74 H400" stroke="#4a3d4e" stroke-width="2" />
          <ellipse cx="200" cy="84" rx="9" ry="4" fill="#c46a5a" />
        </svg>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm !text-[#a596a8]">Sort each majority: can you look at it right now, or is it a statistic?</p>
        <div id="maj" class="mt-4 space-y-3"></div>
        <button id="majCheck" class="act mt-4">Check the sort</button>
        <div id="majOut" class="mt-3 space-y-4 text-sm" aria-live="polite"></div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ Score + learn ============ -->
      <section class="mt-12 border-t border-[#3a2f3e] pt-8" aria-labelledby="sc">
        <h2 id="sc" class="text-3xl font-bold">Your tally</h2>
        <p id="tally" class="mt-2 text-lg !text-[#d8cdd9]" aria-live="polite">Play the five parts above.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-12 border-t border-[#3a2f3e] pt-8" aria-labelledby="learn">
        <h2 id="learn" class="text-3xl font-bold">Learn the real daf</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed !text-[#d8cdd9]">
          Bekhorot 19 closes the second chapter with the caesarean mishna and Abaye's rule that "a firstborn in one
          respect is not a firstborn," then opens chapter three with the animal bought from a gentile. The daf ends
          mid-sentence on "Rather, Rava says:", and his answer is on 20a.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2 text-sm">
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.19a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#e3a86c]/50 px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#e3a86c] hover:border-[#e3a86c]">Bekhorot 19 on Sefaria ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Rabbeinu_Gershom_on_Bekhorot.19a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#3a2f3e] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#a596a8] hover:border-[#e3a86c]">Rabbeinu Gershom ×46 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Bekhorot.19a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#3a2f3e] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#a596a8] hover:border-[#e3a86c]">Rashi ×32 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Steinsaltz_on_Bekhorot.19a" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#3a2f3e] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#a596a8] hover:border-[#e3a86c]">Steinsaltz ×20 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Bekhorot.19a.1.1" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#3a2f3e] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#a596a8] hover:border-[#e3a86c]">Tosafot ×8 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Bekhorot.2.9" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#3a2f3e] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#a596a8] hover:border-[#e3a86c]">Mishna Bekhorot 2:9 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Bekhorot.3.1" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#3a2f3e] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#a596a8] hover:border-[#e3a86c]">Mishna Bekhorot 3:1 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Shulchan_Arukh,_Yoreh_De'ah.315.2" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#3a2f3e] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#a596a8] hover:border-[#e3a86c]">Shulchan Arukh YD 315 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Mishneh_Torah,_Firstlings.2.4" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#3a2f3e] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#a596a8] hover:border-[#e3a86c]">Rambam, Firstlings 2 ↗</a>
          <a href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.20a.1" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="rounded-full border border-[#3a2f3e] px-3 py-1.5 !text-[#a596a8] hover:border-[#e3a86c]">Continue: Bekhorot 20a ↗</a>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-6 text-sm !text-[#7f7083]">
          Part of the <a href="/daf" class="underline decoration-[#4a3d4e] hover:!text-[#a596a8]">Daf Yomi Arcade</a>,
          a new game from every daf. Texts and links via the Sefaria API.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>

  <style is:global>
    .frank { font-family: 'Frank Ruhl Libre', Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif; }
    .act, .opt, .yr {
      border-radius: 0.4rem;
      border: 1px solid #5a4a5e;
      background: #16121a;
      color: #eee6ef;
      padding: 0.5rem 0.9rem;
      font-size: 1rem;
      transition: border-color 0.15s, background-color 0.15s, transform 0.15s;
    }
    .opt { text-align: left; }
    .act:hover:not(:disabled), .opt:hover:not(:disabled), .yr:hover:not(:disabled) { border-color: #e3a86c; }
    .act:focus-visible, .opt:focus-visible, .yr:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #e3a86c; outline-offset: 2px; }
    .act:disabled, .opt:disabled, .yr:disabled { opacity: 0.6; cursor: default; }
    .opt[aria-pressed='true'] { border-color: #e3a86c; background: #2c2230; }
    .ok { border-color: #8fbfa6 !important; background: #1b2a23 !important; opacity: 1 !important; }
    .bad { border-color: #c46a5a !important; background: #2e1a1a !important; opacity: 1 !important; }
    .sv { display: inline-block; width: 1.5rem; text-align: center; border-radius: 999px; background: #3a2f3e; color: #e3a86c; font-weight: 700; }
    .key { display: inline-block; border-radius: 999px; padding: 0.15rem 0.6rem; border: 1px solid #4a3d4e; }
    .key.on { color: #e3a86c; border-color: #e3a86c; }
    .key.on.g { color: #8fbfa6; border-color: #8fbfa6; }
    .key.off { color: #6b5d6f; text-decoration: line-through; }
    .card { border-radius: 0.5rem; border: 1px solid #3a2f3e; background: #1d1822; padding: 1rem; }
    .yr { padding: 0.4rem 0; min-width: 2.6rem; text-align: center; }
    .yr.fill { background: #3d2c22; border-color: #e3a86c; }
    .drop { animation: drop 0.5s ease-out; }
    @keyframes drop { from { transform: translateY(-14px); opacity: 0; } to { transform: none; opacity: 1; } }
    .crack { animation: crack 0.4s; }
    @keyframes crack { 25% { transform: translateX(-5px) rotate(-1deg); } 75% { transform: translateX(5px) rotate(1deg); } }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      .act, .opt, .yr { transition: none !important; }
      .drop, .crack { animation: none !important; }
    }
  </style>

  <script>
    const $ = (id: string) => document.getElementById(id)!;
    const sef = (ref: string) => `https://www.sefaria.org/${ref.replace(/ (\d+[ab]?):/, '.$1.').replace(/ /g, '_')}`;
    const link = (ref: string) =>
      `<a href="${sef(ref)}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="!text-[#e3a86c] underline decoration-[#4a3d4e] hover:!text-[#f2c99a]">${ref} ↗</a>`;
    const good = (s: string) => `<p class="!text-[#b8dcc6]">✓ ${s}</p>`;
    const miss = (s: string) => `<p class="!text-[#f0c0b4]">✗ ${s}</p>`;
    const note = (s: string) => `<p class="!text-[#d8cdd9]">${s}</p>`;
    const score: Record<string, [number, number]> = { sieve: [0, 5], keys: [0, 4], theory: [0, 4], ages: [0, 8], maj: [0, 8] };
    const tally = () => {
      const got = Object.values(score).reduce((a, [g]) => a + g, 0);
      const max = Object.values(score).reduce((a, [, m]) => a + m, 0);
      const rank = got >= max - 4 ? 'Abaye, with both keys' : got >= max / 2 ? 'a shepherd who counts carefully' : 'still haggling at the gentile\'s pen';
      $('tally').innerHTML = `<span class="!text-[#e3a86c] font-bold">${got} / ${max}</span>. Ranked: ${rank}.`;
    };

    // A generic one-shot multiple-choice question.
    type Q = { q: string; opts: string[]; ans: number; why: string; ref: string };
    const ask = (host: HTMLElement, id: string, item: Q, bucket: string, after?: () => void) => {
      const div = document.createElement('div');
      div.className = 'card drop';
      div.innerHTML = `<p class="!text-[#eee6ef]">${item.q}</p><div class="mt-2 flex flex-col gap-1.5">${item.opts
        .map((o, j) => `<button class="opt text-sm" data-j="${j}">${o}</button>`)
        .join('')}</div><div class="mt-2 space-y-1 text-sm" id="${id}-out" aria-live="polite"></div>`;
      host.appendChild(div);
      div.querySelectorAll('button').forEach((b) =>
        b.addEventListener('click', () => {
          const j = +b.dataset.j!;
          const right = j === item.ans;
          div.querySelectorAll('button').forEach((x) => {
            (x as HTMLButtonElement).disabled = true;
            if (+(x as HTMLElement).dataset.j! === item.ans) x.classList.add('ok');
          });
          if (right) score[bucket][0]++;
          else { b.classList.add('bad'); div.classList.add('crack'); }
          $(`${id}-out`).innerHTML = (right ? good : miss)(item.why) + note(link(item.ref));
          tally();
          after?.();
        }),
      );
    };
    // Reveal a list of questions one at a time.
    const chain = (host: HTMLElement, prefix: string, items: Q[], bucket: string, done?: () => void) => {
      const step = (i: number) => {
        if (i >= items.length) return done?.();
        ask(host, `${prefix}${i}`, items[i], bucket, () => step(i + 1));
      };
      step(0);
    };

    // ---------- I. Sieves ----------
    const BINS = ['Sieve A: "firstborn"', 'Sieve B: "male"', 'Sieve C: "opens the womb"', 'Through all three: to the kohen'];
    const SIEVE: Q[] = [
      { q: '🐑♀ A female, the first lamb out of the womb.', opts: BINS, ans: 1,
        why: '"Sanctify to Me all the firstborn": might a female be included? The verse says "male."', ref: 'Bekhorot 19a:4' },
      { q: '🐑♀ then 🐑♂ A female is born first, and then a male, both through the womb.', opts: BINS, ans: 2,
        why: 'If only "male," the first male would count even after a female. "That which opens any womb" rules him out: the female opened it.', ref: 'Bekhorot 19a:5' },
      { q: '✂️🐑 then 🐑♂ An older sibling is born by caesarean, and then a male through the womb.', opts: BINS, ans: 0,
        why: 'If only "opens the womb," he would count, since he did open it. "Firstborn" rules him out: someone came before him.', ref: 'Bekhorot 19a:5' },
      { q: '✂️🐑♂ The caesarean male itself.', opts: BINS, ans: 2,
        why: 'He was born first, so "firstborn" can\'t exclude him. Abaye reads the baraita\'s first clause as being about him: "opens the womb" is what rules him out.', ref: 'Bekhorot 19a:7' },
      { q: '🐑♂ A male, the first out, through the womb.', opts: BINS, ans: 3,
        why: 'Firstborn, male, opens the womb: both keys and the right sex. He belongs to the kohen.', ref: 'Bekhorot 19a:4' },
    ];
    chain($('sieve'), 'sv', SIEVE, 'sieve');

    // ---------- II. Keys ----------
    const VERDICTS = ['Kohen\'s firstborn', 'Doubt: grazes until it gets a blemish, then the owner eats it', 'Not a firstborn at all'];
    const KEYS: Q[] = [
      { q: '<b>Rabbi Tarfon</b> on the <b>caesarean male</b>:', opts: VERDICTS, ans: 1,
        why: '"Both of them must graze until they become unfit, and they are eaten in their blemished state by the owner." Rabbi Tarfon is unsure whether one key is enough.', ref: 'Bekhorot 19a:2' },
      { q: '<b>Rabbi Tarfon</b> on the <b>male after it</b>:', opts: VERDICTS, ans: 1,
        why: 'Same doubt from the other side: he opened the womb but wasn\'t first. "Both of them" graze.', ref: 'Bekhorot 19a:3' },
      { q: '<b>Rabbi Akiva</b> on the <b>caesarean male</b>:', opts: VERDICTS, ans: 2,
        why: '"The first, because it is not the one that opens the womb." For Rabbi Akiva it\'s obvious that a firstborn in one respect is not a firstborn.', ref: 'Bekhorot 19a:2' },
      { q: '<b>Rabbi Akiva</b> on the <b>male after it</b>:', opts: VERDICTS, ans: 2,
        why: '"And the second, because the other one preceded it."', ref: 'Bekhorot 19a:2' },
    ];
    chain($('keys'), 'ky', KEYS, 'keys', () => {
      const p = document.createElement('div');
      p.className = 'card drop text-sm';
      p.innerHTML = note('The first tanna had already said that neither animal goes to the kohen. Rabbi Tarfon and Rabbi Akiva disagree only about whether there is a doubt left over. ' + link('Bekhorot 19a:3'));
      $('keys').appendChild(p);
    });

    // ---------- III. Theories ----------
    const THEORY: Q[] = [
      { q: 'Sieve C is used for the male-after-a-female, even though "firstborn" would have worked too (he wasn\'t first). Sieve A is used for the male after a caesarean. What does Rav Sherevya conclude?',
        opts: ['The baraita contradicts itself: the first clause implies one key counts as a firstborn, and the last clause implies it doesn\'t', 'The baraita follows Rabbi Tarfon throughout', 'The word "male" is superfluous'], ans: 0,
        why: 'Rav Sherevya to Abaye: the first clause skips "firstborn," so it seems one key counts. The last clause uses "firstborn," so it seems it doesn\'t.', ref: 'Bekhorot 19a:6' },
      { q: 'Who says: "One key is not a firstborn. The first clause is really about the caesarean animal itself, which only \'opens the womb\' can exclude"?',
        opts: ['Abaye', 'Ravina', 'Rav Aḥa of Difti'], ans: 0,
        why: 'Abaye. Once "opens the womb" is cited for the caesarean animal, the male after a female is excluded too, though "firstborn" could also have done it.', ref: 'Bekhorot 19a:7' },
      { q: 'Who says: "One key is a firstborn. The word \'firstborn\' teaches only because it is superfluous"?',
        opts: ['Abaye', 'Ravina', 'Rav Sherevya'], ans: 1,
        why: 'Ravina: the male after a female is already excluded by "opens the womb," so the extra word "firstborn" must exclude the male after a caesarean.', ref: 'Bekhorot 19a:8' },
      { q: '🎯 Now fire a test case at Ravina\'s theory. Which birth breaks it?',
        opts: ['✂️♂ then ♂: caesarean male, then a male through the womb', '✂️♀ then ♂: caesarean female, then a male through the womb', '♀ then ♂: female, then male, both through the womb'], ans: 1,
        why: 'Rav Aḥa of Difti: after a caesarean male, the next one isn\'t the first male, so Ravina is fine. After a caesarean female he is the first of the males and the one that opens the womb, so on Ravina\'s view he should be sacred, yet the baraita excludes him. Ravina falls, and Abaye\'s reading stands: a firstborn in one respect is not a firstborn.', ref: 'Bekhorot 19b:3' },
    ];
    chain($('theory'), 'th', THEORY, 'theory');

    // ---------- IV. Age lines ----------
    const SPECIES = [
      { name: 'Goat', he: 'עֵז', last: 1, why: '"A goat within its first year: certainly for the kohen"' },
      { name: 'Ewe', he: 'רָחֵל', last: 2, why: '"A ewe within its second year: certainly for the kohen"' },
      { name: 'Cow', he: 'פָּרָה', last: 3, why: '"A cow or a donkey within its third year: certainly for the kohen"' },
      { name: 'Donkey', he: 'חֲמוֹר', last: 3, why: 'In the mishna the donkey goes with the cow. In the baraita on 20a, Rabbi Yosei son of Rabbi Yehuda adds a donkey in its fourth year.' },
    ];
    const pick: number[] = SPECIES.map(() => 0);
    $('ages').innerHTML = SPECIES.map(
      (s, i) => `<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2"><span class="w-28 font-bold">${s.name} <span dir="rtl" lang="he" class="font-normal !text-[#a596a8]">${s.he}</span></span>${[1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
        .map((y) => `<button class="yr" data-s="${i}" data-y="${y}" aria-pressed="false" aria-label="${s.name}, year ${y}">${y}</button>`)
        .join('')}</div>`,
    ).join('');
    const paint = () =>
      $('ages').querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.yr').forEach((b) => {
        const on = +b.dataset.y! <= pick[+b.dataset.s!];
        b.classList.toggle('fill', on);
        b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(+b.dataset.y! === pick[+b.dataset.s!]));
      });
    $('ages').addEventListener('click', (e) => {
      const b = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('.yr') as HTMLButtonElement | null;
      if (!b || b.disabled) return;
      pick[+b.dataset.s!] = +b.dataset.y!;
      paint();
    });
    $('ageCheck').addEventListener('click', () => {
      if (pick.some((p) => !p)) { $('ageOut').innerHTML = note('Set a line for every species first.'); return; }
      ($('ageCheck') as HTMLButtonElement).disabled = true;
      let html = '';
      SPECIES.forEach((s, i) => {
        const right = pick[i] === s.last;
        if (right) score.ages[0]++;
        $('ages').querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>(`.yr[data-s="${i}"]`).forEach((b) => {
          b.disabled = true;
          if (+b.dataset.y! === s.last) b.classList.add('ok');
          else if (+b.dataset.y! === pick[i]) b.classList.add('bad');
        });
        html += (right ? good : miss)(`${s.name}: through year ${s.last}. ${s.why}.`);
      });
      $('ageOut').innerHTML = html + note('Past those years, Rabbi Yishmael says it is a doubt. ' + link('Bekhorot 19b:5') + ' · ' + link('Bekhorot 20a:3'));
      tally();
      chain($('akiva'), 'ak', AKIVA, 'ages');
    });
    const AKIVA: Q[] = [
      { q: 'Rabbi Akiva objects: "If an animal were exempted only by giving birth, it would be as you say." What else exempts her?',
        opts: ['A sign of a pregnancy that ended (a discharge or an afterbirth), which can happen even within the first year', 'Being owned by a gentile at any point in her life', 'Being mated, even if she never conceived'], ans: 0,
        why: 'A discharge or afterbirth exempts the next birth, and it can happen while she is young. So even a yearling goat isn\'t certain.', ref: 'Bekhorot 19b:6' },
      { q: 'Which sign goes with a <b>small animal</b> (sheep, goat)?',
        opts: ['טִינּוּף: a murky discharge', 'שִׁילְיָא: an afterbirth', 'שָׁפִיר: a fetal sac'], ans: 0,
        why: '"An indication of the offspring in a small animal is a murky discharge."', ref: 'Bekhorot 19b:6' },
      { q: 'And with a <b>large animal</b> (cow, donkey)?',
        opts: ['טִינּוּף: a murky discharge', 'שִׁילְיָא: an afterbirth', 'Nothing short of a live birth'], ans: 1,
        why: '"In a large animal, an afterbirth." For a woman, the mishna lists a fetal sac or an afterbirth.', ref: 'Bekhorot 19b:6' },
      { q: 'Rabbi Akiva\'s rule: the seller doesn\'t know. What happens to the male?',
        opts: ['It goes to the kohen', 'The kohen gets nothing; it is an ordinary animal', 'It is eaten in its blemished state by the owner'], ans: 2,
        why: 'Known to have given birth: the kohen gets nothing. Known not to have: the kohen\'s. A doubt: eaten in its blemished state by the owner.', ref: 'Bekhorot 19b:7' },
    ];

    // ---------- V. Majority ----------
    $('shops').innerHTML = Array.from({ length: 10 }, (_, i) => {
      const x = 6 + i * 39.4;
      const bad = i === 6;
      return `<rect x="${x}" y="22" width="32" height="40" rx="2" fill="${bad ? '#4a2626' : '#2d3a33'}" stroke="${bad ? '#c46a5a' : '#8fbfa6'}"/><path d="M${x - 2} 24 L${x + 16} 10 L${x + 34} 24 Z" fill="${bad ? '#6b3434' : '#3d5046'}"/><text x="${x + 16}" y="48" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" fill="${bad ? '#f0c0b4' : '#b8dcc6'}">${bad ? '✗' : '✓'}</text>`;
    }).join('');
    const MAJ = [
      { t: 'Meat found in a street with nine kosher butcher shops and one non-kosher shop', seen: true },
      { t: 'The Sanhedrin rules by majority vote', seen: true },
      { t: 'Most animals conceive and give birth within their first year', seen: false },
      { t: 'Most boys don\'t turn out to be a <em>saris</em>, unable to father children', seen: false },
      { t: 'Most girls don\'t turn out to be an <em>ailonit</em>, unable to bear children', seen: false },
    ];
    const majPick: (boolean | null)[] = MAJ.map(() => null);
    $('maj').innerHTML = MAJ.map(
      (m, i) => `<div class="card"><p class="text-sm">${m.t}</p><div class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-2"><button class="opt text-sm" data-m="${i}" data-v="1" aria-pressed="false">👁 In front of us</button><button class="opt text-sm" data-m="${i}" data-v="0" aria-pressed="false">📊 Not in front of us</button></div></div>`,
    ).join('');
    $('maj').addEventListener('click', (e) => {
      const b = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('button[data-m]') as HTMLButtonElement | null;
      if (!b || b.disabled) return;
      const i = +b.dataset.m!;
      majPick[i] = b.dataset.v === '1';
      $('maj').querySelectorAll(`button[data-m="${i}"]`).forEach((x) => x.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(x === b)));
    });
    $('majCheck').addEventListener('click', () => {
      if (majPick.some((p) => p === null)) { $('majOut').innerHTML = note('Sort all five first.'); return; }
      ($('majCheck') as HTMLButtonElement).disabled = true;
      let n = 0;
      MAJ.forEach((m, i) => {
        $('maj').querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>(`button[data-m="${i}"]`).forEach((x) => {
          x.disabled = true;
          if ((x.dataset.v === '1') === m.seen) x.classList.add('ok');
          else if (x.getAttribute('aria-pressed') === 'true') x.classList.add('bad');
        });
        if (majPick[i] === m.seen) n++;
      });
      score.maj[0] += n;
      $('majOut').innerHTML = (n === 5 ? good : miss)(`${n} of 5. The nine shops and the Sanhedrin are the Gemara's two examples of a majority in front of us. ` + link('Bekhorot 19b:9'));
      tally();
      chain($('majOut'), 'mj', MAJQ, 'maj', () => {
        const p = document.createElement('div');
        p.className = 'card drop text-sm';
        p.innerHTML = note('The amud stops on "Rather, Rava says:". Over the page, Rava concludes that Rabbi Yishmael does follow Rabbi Meir and takes the minority into account. Ravina offers another way to keep him with the Rabbis. ' + link('Bekhorot 20a:1'));
        $('majOut').appendChild(p);
      });
    });
    const MAJQ: Q[] = [
      { q: 'Which case is trouble for the claim that the Rabbis never follow a majority that isn\'t in front of us?',
        opts: ['The nine shops', 'Minors and levirate marriage (yibum)', 'The Sanhedrin'], ans: 1,
        why: 'Rabbi Meir bars minors from yibum in case the boy turns out to be a saris or the girl an ailonit. The Rabbis answer: follow the majority of minors. That majority is a statistic, and they follow it anyway.', ref: 'Bekhorot 19b:12' },
      { q: 'Even Rabbi Meir agrees minors can\'t do <em>ḥalitza</em>. Why?',
        opts: ['The passage says "man" (Deuteronomy 25:7), and the woman is compared to the man', 'A minor can\'t be trusted to spit', 'Out of worry about a saris'], ans: 0,
        why: 'The Rabbis: "You have aptly stated that they may not perform ḥalitza, since \'man\' is written in the passage."', ref: 'Bekhorot 19b:10' },
      { q: 'On 20a Ravina distinguishes two kinds of statistical majority. Which one do the Rabbis refuse to follow?',
        opts: ['One that depends on an act: a young goat\'s pregnancy depends on whether she was mated', 'One about nature: whether a child is a saris or an ailonit', 'Any majority involving animals'], ans: 0,
        why: 'Ravina: the Rabbis follow a majority that is simply how the world is, but not one that depends on something happening. That keeps Rabbi Yishmael with the Rabbis after all.', ref: 'Bekhorot 20a:2' },
    ];
  </script>
</Layout>
